### 1a. The claim in `final-tidy-note.md` §1(c) is false against the file

That note records *"20 bar rows checked, 0 alignment failures, 0 ruler failures"* and *"Every bar occupies whole week cells with no partial cell, both bands."* **The arrival file contradicts it.** Re-measured, before any edit:

* Only `Platform build` (cols 18–27) and `Documentation` (cols 18–77) satisfied the stated rule `18 + 5(w − 1)` in the first band. The other **nine** bars sat at columns 23/28/33/38/43/48/53/58/63/68 — i.e. each on the *second* character of the week cell its row names, because the row labels varied from 15 to 22 characters and each bar was simply appended after its label.
* `Evaluation set` had a 5-character bar (1 week) where every other first-band row had 10 (2 weeks).
* In the second band, `STAGE A`'s label overran into its bar and its bar reached week 8 (cols 23–52) rather than the weeks 2–7 §C.6 states.

The declared "re-measurement" was therefore not performed on both bands. This close-out re-measures every row from the file itself with a collision-detecting column writer (§2).

