## 2. The chart as delivered — full census

**Ruler invariant, verified against the actual ruler line, not assumed.** The delivered ruler is

```
               W1   W2   W3   W4   W5   W6   W7   W8   W9  W10  W11  W12
```

`W1`'s `W` is at column 16; each week is a five-character cell; every row label is right-padded to 20 characters; column 21 is therefore **both** the first column of `W1`'s cell and the column at which every bar starts. So **week `w` begins at column `21 + 5(w − 1)`**:

| week | W1 | W2 | W3 | W4 | W5 | W6 | W7 | W8 | W9 | W10 | W11 | W12 |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| cell | 21–25 | 26–30 | 31–35 | 36–40 | 41–45 | 46–50 | 51–55 | 56–60 | 61–65 | 66–70 | 71–75 | 76–80 |

The ruler line is 72 characters and its characters fall in exactly those cells; every gate marker and every bar was then written **by column index** with a collision detector, so no row can overlap its own label or a neighbouring segment.

