## 3. Resolution of the Stage C span ambiguity — the authoritative span

**The authoritative Stage C span is weeks 8–10, and it is not ambiguous once §C.6's own convention is applied.**

§C.6 states the convention in the paragraph immediately before its stage table: *"A stage's week span … is therefore the span of its **build-and-cover sequence**, and its **coverage portion cannot begin before week 7** … So a stage's coverage begins at **the later of week 7 and its entry gate** … Every span runs **through** the stage's exit-gate week."*

Applying it to §C.6's own Stage C row:

* Stage C's entry gate is that **Stage B is exited**, which §C.6 and §F.1 both put at **G3, week 8**.
* Stage C's exit gate is **G4, week 10**.
* So Stage C's *coverage* portion is **weeks 8–10**; its build runs earlier; its **overall span** — which is what the table's `Weeks` column states and what a bar must therefore draw — is **weeks 8–10**.

The two reported readings are resolved as follows: *"the stage window is weeks 8–10 with the build in weeks 3–7"* is the correct reading; *"its overall bar is weeks 7–10"* was produced by prepending the final week of the build (`=`) to the coverage run, which makes the bar wider than the span the table states. §C.6 itself says *"Weeks 8–10. Build in weeks 3–7 … covered in weeks 8–10"*, and §F.2's weekly plan agrees (device work weeks 2–8, drift baseline for Cisco components week 10). The chart now draws **weeks 8–10**.

The short proposal confirms it independently: `FYP-Proposal-SHORT.md` §7.2 states Stage C as **"Weeks 8-10"** with the AI-side closure at **G4 (week 10)** — the same span and the same coverage window.

**Edit made.** §C.6's Stage C weeks cell said *"**Weeks 8–10.** Build in weeks 3–7 … covered in weeks 8–10"*, which reads as if the span were a coverage window only and leaves the overall span implicit — the gap that produced the two readings. The cell now reads *"**Weeks 8–10 as the stage's overall build-and-cover span** … its **coverage** portion is weeks 8–10 only … so §F.3's band draws `STAGE C` as a `#` bar covering weeks 8–10 (columns 56–70)"*, and it records that the short proposal states the same span. The convention is now also stated explicitly in §F.3's prose (§4).

