## 4. Prose-rule check

**The prose's ruler arithmetic was wrong or unverifiable on arrival and is now exactly right.** Checks:

| Check | Arrival | Now |
|---|---|---|
| Ruler arithmetic | *"the `W` of `W1` sits in column 18 … `18 + 5(w − 1)`"* — **true of the arrival ruler line**, so the arithmetic was not itself false | *"the `W` of `W1` sits in column 21 … `21 + 5(w − 1)`"* — matches the delivered ruler line |
| Cells listed | `W1` 18–22 … `W12` 73–77 | `W1` 21–25 … `W12` 76–80 — verified against the ruler |
| Gate columns | `G1` 28, `G2` 43, `G3` 53; **`G4` was omitted**, though a `G4` marker existed | `G1` 31, `G2` 46, `G3` 56, **`G4` 66**; `G2-H` 46 named on its own row |
| Right edge | *"no bar extends past column 77"* — **false on arrival**: `Documentation` and `Monitoring + syslog` both ended at column 77 (true only by accident of their last bar landing there), and three rows wrote label text into week cells | *"no bar extends past column 80"*, the right edge of `W12`; verified per row |
| *"every gate marker and every bar begins at the first character of its own week's cell"* | **False on arrival** for 9 of 16 first-band bars and for 2 of 4 stage bars | **True**, and asserted as re-measured; every bar's first character is at `21 + 5(w − 1)` |
| *"each row of both bands was re-measured character by character … with no partial cell"* | **False on arrival** (see §1a) | Now true; the note records the earlier claim as false |
| Legend | **Absent** — no legend existed anywhere in the document | Added: blank = not yet built; `.` = planned but not yet begun; `=` = built or verified but not yet AI-covered; `#` = AI-covered. States that a stage bar is read as one bar, that its overall span is §C.6's span, and that the `=`/`#` boundary is never earlier than week 7 |
| Glyph enumeration | Prose said *"Three characters, so that neither axis is lost"* but named only `#` and `=`, and used a third glyph (`.`) undeclared | The prose now defines **all four glyph states — the three characters `.` `=` `#` plus the blank — explicitly and once**, and says which band each appears in. The inaccurate three-character enumeration is gone |

**A defect of the previous prose that mattered:** it claimed a re-measurement of both bands that the file shows was not done, and it certified 0 failures. That sentence is now a true statement of what this close-out did, and §1a of this note records the discrepancy rather than leaving the earlier claim standing unqualified.

